=== intro

A message on your private channel. No sender ID. Just coordinates in the lower docks and a time.

When you arrive, a figure in worn but expensive clothes is waiting. "Your ship. Your discretion. My cargo. Destination: Shadow Market. Payment on delivery. Interested?"

* [Accept the job]
  ~ addCard cargo_contraband
  ~ flag smuggling_active
  ~ chronicle "Shadow Work"
    Accepted unmarked cargo for delivery to the Shadow Market. No questions asked. None answered.
  -> END

* [Ask what's in the containers]
  -> clarification

* [Refuse firmly]
  ~ flag refused_smuggling
  ~ chronicle "Principles"
    Turned down contraband work. Some lines we don't cross.
  -> END

=== clarification

The figure smiles thinly. "Contents are need-to-know, captain. Your job is transport, not inventory.

"But since you ask—nothing that explodes, nothing that screams, nothing that the Collective would want. That's all you're getting."

* [Good enough—accept]
  ~ addCard cargo_contraband
  ~ flag smuggling_active
  ~ chronicle "Shadow Work"
    Accepted unmarked cargo. "Nothing that explodes, nothing that screams." Cold comfort, but comfort enough.
  -> END

* [Not good enough—refuse]
  ~ flag refused_smuggling_twice
  -> END
